WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.914
Emperor Yongzheng was one of the most hardworking emperors of the Qing dynasty.

00:00:03.914 --> 00:00:08.041
He reviewed many memorials every day and often worked late into the night.

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:11.207
His desk was always piled high with memorials.

00:00:11.583 --> 00:00:14.832
He reformed the tax laws and carried out the reform merging the head tax into the land tax.

00:00:14.832 --> 00:00:18.548
From then on, taxes were calculated based on land, which was fairer.

00:00:18.548 --> 00:00:21.642
The elders in the village said this was truly fair.

00:00:21.642 --> 00:00:25.067
For common people without land, the burden became lighter.

00:00:25.067 --> 00:00:27.703
He gave officials integrity-nourishing silver to encourage honesty and integrity.

00:00:28.688 --> 00:00:32.232
Officials' salaries increased, and corruption decreased.

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:36.285
The state treasury gradually filled up, and the granaries were full.

00:00:36.285 --> 00:00:39.827
Granaries and silver treasuries are both foundations of the state.

00:00:39.827 --> 00:00:42.695
He established a new administrative office to handle state affairs.

00:00:42.723 --> 00:00:47.037
Ministers were on standby at all times, and efficiency improved.

00:00:47.037 --> 00:00:50.315
This small room became the center of the court.

00:00:50.315 --> 00:00:53.977
Yongzheng's reforms strengthened central administration.

00:00:53.977 --> 00:00:56.059
They also laid the foundation for the prosperous age that followed.
